A release that changes no table: nothing to plan, and the database still
moves to the new release, so the next release's lines know where it is.
An `init!` task hears it came from release 3.

== before
CREATE TABLE dish (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, name TEXT NOT NULL) STRICT;
PRAGMA user_version = 3;

== after
-- @release 4
CREATE TABLE dish (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, name TEXT NOT NULL) STRICT;

== plan
migrated from release 3

== query
PRAGMA user_version

== rows
4
